WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
In 2014, Brazil left the UN's Hunger Map:

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.210
undernourishment had
fallen below 2.5 per cent.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.450
Between 2019 and 2022, it was back on.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.510
In 2025, it left again.

5
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.550
Singapore imports over
90 per cent of its food,

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.390
with about 1 per cent
of its land for farming.

7
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.850
So what does it take to end
hunger, and keep it ended?

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.110
Grow more food?

9
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.550
Plant GM crops?

10
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.490
In this mission, you'll weigh
solutions at every scale,

11
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.930
from food waste to
France's supermarket law.

12
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.290
Then you'll evaluate new
technologies: GM crops,

13
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.830
Golden Rice, vertical
farming and cell-grown meat.

14
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.690
Your mission: decide what
it takes to end hunger,

15
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.430
and to keep it ended.
